The sensation of his first 'Door Crossing' in some time wasn't strong enough to make him feel nostalgic.

To begin with, that spatial teleportation through a door came with almost no real feeling of having traversed space. Just like walking in and out of a room normally, one's stride simply carried them past the connection between spaces.

That was why, at that moment, the breath that inadvertently leaked from Subaru's mouth wasn't due to deep feelings about the 'Door Crossing', but rather his reaction to looking out across the room they had been ushered into.

"This is... a bizarre room that practically screams 'a witch would love this'."

It was a uniquely structured chamber, with windows running the entire circumference of the walls. It was a spacious room, and likely at the castle's very top—the presence of the blue sky spreading beyond the windows and the white clouds drifting beneath it faintly informed him of the room's relative position. The scenery outside wasn't the endlessly falling strange space still fresh in Subaru's memory, but the sky of the surface world itself.

That was, in other words, proof that Tiga's words hadn't been a lie.

"A floating castle, Kugelschreiber, huh... Once you get your hands on an airborne vehicle, it really starts to feel like the late-game of an RPG, but don't you guys get that feeling?"

"I don't know what you're talking about, but it sounds like it doesn't matter. More importantly, look."

"――Subaru!"

Responding coldly to Subaru's marveling, Ferris pointed straight ahead, and Beatrice came dashing over from the back of the room with a patter of footsteps, the hem of her dress fluttering.

With Crusch on his back, Subaru caught Beatrice with his chest as she leaped at him from the front. Somehow managing to hold his ground, he felt a wave of relief seeing that she was unharmed at a glance.

"Beako, I'm glad you're safe. What a relief."

"That is Betty's line, I suppose! We got separated like that, and on top of that, you ignored Betty's voice and ran off, so I was worried sick, in fact!"

"That wasn't my fault, it was because of the dirty trick the enemy pulled... Anyway, we all somehow managed to make it through safe on our end. Anything happen on your end... well, obviously something did."

"I suppose. ――Betty moved the castle, in fact."

Placing her hands on her hips, Beatrice nodded with a smug look on her face. Her proud demeanor was cute, but the cause-and-effect relationship between the situation up until a moment ago and moving the castle was a mystery to Subaru.

So, contrary to the romance of a flying castle, there were plenty of doubts about that decision, but――

"Moving the castle was my decision, made in consultation with the 'Librarian'. There was a fear that the entrance we used to come and go had been seized by the enemy, and an ambush was lying in wait."

So, taking over for Beatrice, Russell answered Subaru's doubts, standing in the center of the room.

In the center of the spacious room stood a round pedestal large enough for several adults to gather around; above it floated a strange black sphere, and Russell was holding his hands over it.

It was some sort of fantasy apparatus, but it seemed he couldn't step away from it, so Subaru and the others walked over to him instead.

"This, engraved on the pedestal... is it a world map?"

"Yes, that seems to be the case in general. However, because the era in which it was carved is somewhat old, there are many points that differ from the current world map. It poses little inconvenience, though."

Peering at the circular pedestal, carved upon its surface was a world map rendered in relief—just as Russell had answered, it appeared to depict an era older than the present.

Considering the history of Kugelschreiber Castle, it was likely a map from over four hundred years ago. A desire to bring a current world map and compare the two welled up inside him, but,

"Leaving that for later... Russell-san, what's this about an ambush?"

"Call me 'Silver Fox'. ――It is a natural deduction. The path of teleportation whose value had significantly fallen even in my eyes, and the 'Beloved Children' who had infiltrated the castle... Assuming the other side to be few in number would be unreasonable."

"Most likely, some bastard eager for credit tried to jump the gun, didn't he? There's always someone who can't fall in line, no matter where you go. Especially since not a single one of those 'Beloved Children' seems to have any sense of camaraderie anyway."

Following up on Russell's answer, Rachins glanced at Melty and 'Black Dog' beside him.

Even if being former 'Beloved Children' was the truth, Subaru wanted to defend the two against that unfair evaluation, but putting Melty aside, it was hard to make excuses for 'Black Dog's rather weak sense of camaraderie.

"Even so, thanks to the bond we've forged over these past two months, we were able to repel the enemy. Right, 'Black Dog'?"

"A bond—? Woah-woah, don't go spoutin' such disgustin', sickening crap! It was pure coin-ci-dence, a miracle! We're jus'— fellows who happen to hate the same bastards, ain't we—?"

"See? Just like this, we get along fine. There's a lot of guys here you can't reason with, after all."

Subaru shrugged at 'Black Dog', who was giving him a double thumbs-down. Rachins looked as if he had an objection to Subaru's interpretation, but unable to find any point in arguing it right there, he concluded it on his own with a "Whatever," and,

"Anyway, to avoid an ambush, we moved around and joined up with the 'Librarian'. This girl wanted to go look for you bastards, but..."

"We explained the situation and discussed a counterproposal. As a result, we thought that if their ambush posture were disrupted, the other side would be forced to change their response――"

"Betty moved Mother's castle, I suppose."

With the train of thought of the members who had been acting separately sorted out, Subaru finally understood.

All that remained was how to move this castle in order to put that conclusion into practice, but――

"Does that black sphere 'Silver Fox' has been holding his hands over this whole time have something to do with it?"

"Yes. Though the precise principles are unknown, it is a mechanism where the castle moves by reflecting the will of the pilot. However, without the 'Librarian', it is doubtful whether we would have found the method of activation."

"I see. Good girl, good girl, you're a lifesaver to all of us."

"Naturally, in fact. ...Though, not being by your side made Betty anxious, I suppose."

Pinching the hem of Subaru's clothes slightly, Beatrice lowered her eyes, looking endearing. Even if it was something she could accept as a plan to break through the situation, putting off rushing to where Subaru was after getting separated must have taken a great deal of courage for Beatrice as well.

He was glad that Beatrice's courageous decision hadn't gone to waste.

"Um, I understand the circumstances. But is flying a castle really alright? Won't we stand out way too much and end up being pursued the whole time...?"

"Of course, we have already discussed that point. 'Librarian', this castle has――"

"A 'Cognitive Disruption' effect placed upon it, in fact. It will not be putting on a flashy, gaudy parade across the sky endlessly, I suppose. However, those with sharp intuition or someone who has boarded the castle once might see through the effect, so overconfidence is forbidden, in fact."

"However, having rumors surface is not entirely disadvantageous. The ones whose attention we wish to draw are not limited to the enemy, after all."

"That's..."

Subaru's eyes widened at Russell's words, and Russell gave him a quiet nod. ――The ones whose attention they wanted to catch with a conspicuous castle were without a doubt their allies, with whom they currently had no way to make contact.

Aside from Emilia and the others whose whereabouts were known, Rem and Otto's group who had vanished, and Roswaal's group who had gone into hiding beforehand were all in a state where contact was impossible. Subaru and the others moving with the 'Six Tongues' had no means of getting in touch with their separated companions either.

However, if information about the floating castle spread, for better or worse, it would make it easier to take action.

"Roswaal can fly under his own power, so he might just hop right aboard."

"To be frank, we cannot deny hoping for that. We are maintaining quite an altitude, but if it is Roswaal, he should be able to reach us without freezing."

"Besides, if it is Roswaal, freezing a little would serve as good medicine, I suppose."

"Yeah, you're trashing him, but it's totally deserved."

Though Roswaal was thoroughly roasted by the two who had deep ties with him, Russell and Beatrice, there was no denying it was his own fault, so Subaru didn't offer any follow-up either.

At any rate, the circumstances of how the castle flew and the concerns regarding having flown it were mostly resolved.

All that was left was――

"If we have a little time right now, I'd like to explain what happened on our end... and Beako, is there a room where Crusch can rest?"

"There should probably be an unransacked guest room, in fact. Betty will guide you, I suppose."

"Roger that. Then, Ferris would probably rather stay with her, so can I leave the report to Mel... 'White Sheep'-chan and 'Black Dog'? Once that's done――"

"Yes, please leave the report to us. ――After that, let us speak."

Placing a hand over her chest, Melty gave a deep nod, her face quiet yet harboring resolve.

Dwelling within her round eyes was a will, in contrast to her lovely and dainty features, that was exceptionally strong, sharp, and unyielding like diamond――

"――About what I am fighting for."

"――There is a land called Faradar. That is where I am from... A remote land where the Evil Eye Tribe has lived for generations."

So, speaking in an intentionally detached voice, Melty began to recount her past.

This was after they had arranged the most decent guest room in the castle and let Crusch rest there. Leaving the sleeping Crusch to Ferris, Subaru and the others set up the second-most decent guest room as a place for discussion, and there they were listening to the promised story from Melty.

The precious, secret story that lay between her and 'Black Dog'—as well as Tiga and Pooka.

"When you say the Evil Eye Tribe, there seemed to be a few of them scattered around Vollachia. A demi-human race that could use special, Divine Protection-like powers, right? Melty-chan, you too?"

"Yes, that understanding is correct. Faradar was also a settlement in the remote regions of the Vollachian Empire, and I am one of the Evil Eye Tribe... I spoke to you about the power of my Evil Eye, didn't I, Subaru-san?"

"Yeah, 'Bewitchment', which makes anyone you touch feel affection toward you, right?"

Nodding slightly, Melty answered Subaru's confirmation with a serious expression.

'Bewitchment'—just from the phrasing alone, it didn't sound like a grave power, but during their activities with the 'Six Tongues' so far, he had frequently seen Russell rely on it. Indeed, she had even been chosen as one of the 'Beloved Children'. It undoubtedly held that much potency.

As if to back that up, Beatrice, who was holding hands with Subaru, murmured, "'Bewitchment'..."

"Betty has heard of it, in fact. Among the Evil Eye Tribe created in an attempt to replicate the Authorities of the 'Witches', it was the 'Evil Eye of Calamity' that best suited that purpose... or so it was supposed to be, I suppose."

"You, you're always being pretty by my side, yet you drop bombshells out of nowhere from time to time, don't you? What's this about replicating the Authorities of the 'Witches'?"

"It is a story from the era of the 'Witch War', and Betty has no real recollection of it either, in fact. It is just that, back then, 'Witches' were running rampant all over the place, and that was one of the countermeasures against them, I suppose. If you wish to know, Betty will tell you next time, so for now, concentrate on 'White Sheep'... on Melty's story, in fact."

"Dammit, that's a promise, got it...?! Melty-chan, sorry for interrupting. Go ahead."

"Yes. But just as the 'Librarian'-san says, my power was called something like that. It was an effect that hadn't appeared in our clan for hundreds of years, and it was said to be a long-cherished wish. ...I am aware that it is that frightening a power. But that awareness wasn't enough."

In front of Subaru and Beatrice, Melty placed a hand against her chest, her brows drooping.

Harboring strong self-reproach and remorse over it having not been enough, she let out a small breath,

"When I was little, I was indifferent to my own power, and because of that, I caused conflicts and made a terrible mess of things. I deeply regretted that... But the true regret came right after."

"Regret... Don't tell me... catching Capella's eye?"

"That too, is part of it. ...However, the greatest regret was not that."

"――――"

"...It is Tiga."

Taking a beat of hesitation, Melty then broached the main topic.

Tiga Rauleon—a member of the 'Divine Dragon Church', Subaru's 'my friend', someone on his wavelength he could really talk to, and the man considered an 'Executor' affiliated with the enemy 'Beloved Children'.

As for the extraordinary relationship that lay between that Tiga and Melty――

"It was when both he and I were children. A traveling troupe of performers visited Faradar. Tiga was a member of that troupe... and having been kept away from people because I couldn't handle the power of 'Bewitchment' well, I happened to meet Tiga. And then..."

"...And then?"

"――With the power of 'Bewitchment', I wished for him to stay by my side. That is what I let myself want."

Clutching the front of her clothes tightly, Melty spoke as if making a confession of guilt.

Melty stressed again that she had been a young child. Endowed with tremendous power from birth, she was ignorant of its restraint and proper usage. Melty was not so selfish that she could excuse herself by calling it a mistake brought about by those things.

"Tiga left the troupe that was his family and remained in Faradar. Innocently, I rejoiced at that... and dragged Tiga into this hell."

"Hell, I suppose. That would be the 'Beloved Children' of the Sin Archbishop of 'Lust', in fact."

"――Yes. When Mama found me and was taking me away, in order to be with me... to grant my 'request', I do not know what conditions Tiga presented. But in order to be favored by that Mama, how he sold away his own life piece by piece...!"

Her already fair skin gone deathly pale, Melty let the end of her words tremble feebly.

The regret and shame swirling within her heart were transmitted vividly and clearly to Subaru. If Subaru were to drag someone precious to him—Emilia, Rem, Garfiel, Petra, and the others—into an inescapable hell because of his own mistake, he would regret it too.

"Betty and Otto were not in your consideration, I suppose."

"Well, you and Otto have already given me permission to drag you into hell..."

"It is a relief that you seem to understand, in fact. However, being on the same level as Otto is something Betty will have words with Otto about when we regroup later, I suppose."

Apparently, some such determination had been made inside Beatrice. It seemed likely that Subaru would be on the receiving end of complaints from Otto after Beatrice had words with him once they regrouped, but well, that was fine.

At any rate, he understood the guilt Melty held toward Tiga, as well as the connection between the two. He understood, but there was something he didn't understand.

"I get that Tiga has that deep of a connection with you, Melty-chan. But his attitude when we ran into him in the castle's basement was the complete opposite of that explanation. That was..."

"――He does not, remember. Me."

"――――"

"Tiga has forgotten about me. ...No, it is not just Tiga. Mama, the 'Beloved Children', people all over the world, have forgotten me. ――That is the reason I was able to leave the 'Beloved Children' like this now."

At that answer from Melty, Beatrice, whose hand was clasped in his, squeezed slightly tighter. Discerning the meaning behind it, Subaru gave a small nod to show he understood.

To be honest, even before hearing this story, he had harbored suspicions that it might be so.

Considering the relationship with Tiga recounted from Melty's mouth—given a bond that long and deep, wasn't that the only way to explain how the two of them treated each other now?

However, if that was the case――

"Those 'Gluttony' pieces of shit, not only did they give me and my Rem's relationship a compound fracture, they went and smeared their filth all over Melty-chan's pure love too...?!"

"It is not limited to Subaru and Rem, in fact. Julius, the residents of Priestella... there is no end to it if you start counting the people affected, I suppose."

"In the end, the culprit behind the captured Roy being killed is still unknown too, they just keep scattering mysteries everywhere. Just Melty-chan being able to escape the 'Beloved Children' is nowhere near enough to pay back that debt."

In the first place, Capella, who had tormented Melty, was a Sin Archbishop as well, so it was practically a self-made problem created between Sin Archbishops. There was nothing worthy of being called an achievement.

However, while Subaru fumed over it, Melty blushed faintly,

"U-Um, calling it pure love is a bit..."

"Eh? It's not? But the exchange with Tiga earlier was completely――"

He recalled the skirmish between Melty and Tiga when they had encountered each other underground.

Gazing at Tiga when he appeared, standing in his way as he tried to flee, and her voice that regrettably failed to reach his retreating back—all of it had to be the work of strong affection.

At Subaru's question, Melty let out a flustered "Uuu..." for a while, and,

"N-No comment, please... Besides, for me..."

"――. Look, this might be unsolicited advice, or rather, I think it's better to say it so I'm gonna say it, but if you're thinking you don't have the right to fall in love with someone, Melty-chan, or wondering what right you have to say Tiga is precious to you, you're overthinking it, so you don't need to think that way."

"H-How did you know?! Subaru-san, are you an esper...?!"

"Not to toot my own horn, but Subaru-san is pretty sharp when it comes to other people's business."

"It really is rich to say that about yourself, in fact..."

Brushing off Beatrice's interjection from beside him, Subaru cleared his throat with an "Ahem" in front of the wide-eyed Melty.

When it came to relationships between men and women, there wasn't much advice Subaru could offer to others, but even so, when a visibly pointless struggle was happening, its root had to be severed.

"I have a deep understanding of girls who think they don't have the right to be loved by others. After all, Emilia-tan, Rem, and Beako were all like that. ...Is Beako a bit of a variant? Just to be safe, I'll say it. Beako, I love you."

"Betty loves you too, I suppose. You do not need to say it right now, in fact."

"Drawing courage from such an understanding Beako, I'll continue, but... worrying about whether you have the right to be loved or not is pointless. Anyone has the right to be loved. The only exceptions are Sin Archbishops."

"Subaru-san..."

"I said it earlier, but I'm not going to be swayed by you, Melty-chan. So, me thinking your visuals are good, or your voice is cute, has nothing to do with the power of 'Bewitchment'."

"I-Is that really true? You haven't been bewitched?!"

"Not bewitched, not bewitched. 'Those visuals are great, I could look at that forever'—I even think that about Ferris. I'd get an extremely disgusted look if I said it, so I won't, though. Beako, you're insanely cute too. I could gaze at you for eternity."

"That is the work of Betty's charms, I suppose. There is no power of 'Bewitchment', in fact."

Looking back and forth between Subaru nodding and Beatrice puffing out her chest cutely, Melty blinked repeatedly, and then let out a soft sigh.

It felt as though she was exhaling the heavy weight that had occupied her chest until just moments before.

"The two of you are incredible, aren't you...?"

"Well, we're partners of destiny who have overcome quite a few trials, after all."

"I suppose. We are battle-hardened veterans, in fact."

The height and number of hurdles they had cleared were entirely different, so Subaru and Beatrice stood proud.

Of course, that didn't mean the hardships and suffering Melty had tasted were made any lighter, nor were they being taken lightly. It was doubtful whether it even served as a minor comfort.

Even so, Melty wore a faint smile on her lips,

"I will be sure to remember it. ――That even I might have the right to be loved."

It was an answer characteristic of a girl who was still slightly lacking in confidence.

However, giving her confidence in the truest sense was surely not Subaru's job. The man who had to fulfill that duty was currently in the enemy camp.

Yet, while he now understood that a complicated, yet impenetrable and solid past lay between Melty and Tiga――

"If that's the case, what kind of relationship do you and 'Black Dog' have, Melty-chan? 'Black Dog' was supposed to have a connection with that spirit named Pooka too, so while we're at it, can I dig into this a bit?"

Taking advantage of Melty having finished her recollection regarding 'Bewitchment', Subaru stepped into an area he had been somewhat curious about, but had read the room and refrained from asking until now.

――'Black Dog', who had left the 'Beloved Children' together with Melty and joined the 'Six Tongues'.

For all the spiteful things he said, it was obvious that he cared about Melty. To begin with, 'Black Dog' had a foul mouth toward everyone, so the special treatment for Melty glimpsed in the parts where he wasn't like that was, needless to say, unmistakable.

However, once Tiga's existence entered the picture, it became quite complicated.

"I don't know whose side I should take, my friend Tiga or our current ally 'Black Dog'. Melty-chan, are you some kind of sinful woman?"

"S-Sinful! As I thought, I don't have the right to be loved...!"

"It was just banter, I suppose. Do not take it seriously, in fact. Subaru, do not trouble Melty either, I suppose. Bad boy, in fact."

Because he had said something unnecessary, he received a stern scolding from Beatrice. However, taking a deep breath, Melty cast her eyes down with a "Well," and began,

"...Actually, I truly do not understand the relationship between 'Black Dog' and myself."

"Does that mean... you've forgotten 'Black Dog', Melty-chan?"

"That is part of it, but... it seems 'Black Dog' himself doesn't understand who he is either. As for his relationship with me, well, he only knows that we were together from the beginning."

"Eh... It's not that 'Black Dog' is hiding his relationship with you, Melty-chan?"

"I don't think it is. I don't think he's the kind of person who is clever enough for that..."

That was an answer that contained a great deal of wanting to believe rather than absolute certainty. However, Subaru agreed with Melty's thought on that. 'Black Dog' possessed a personality ill-suited for deceit.

However, taking those as premises, an unnatural situation surfaced.

"Forgotten by those around him, and having forgotten about himself... That's――"

"It matches the result of both one's 'Name' and 'Memories' being devoured by the Authority of 'Gluttony', I suppose. However, if both had been eaten, it would be impossible, in fact."

"Yeah. ...It'd be weird if he wasn't in the same state as Rem when she was a 'Sleeping Beauty'."

If they were to believe Melty's testimony, 'Black Dog's situation was identical to Rem's, who had been attacked by 'Gluttony' and fallen into a long slumber—it should have been the same as the people who still had not awakened in Priestella. And yet, 'Black Dog' had not fallen into a comatose state, and was walking around of his own will.

Could it be that, this late in the game, a new variation among the victims of the Authority of 'Gluttony' had been discovered?

"But if that's the case, the relationship between 'Black Dog' and Pooka makes sense. In other words, those two were originally in a contractual relationship, but neither remembers it. That's why they're missing each other... Same as how Julius's contract with Ia and the others never came undone, right?"

"That is the most convincing explanation, I suppose. ...However, if that is the case, it is pitiable, in fact."

"Pitiable..."

"To be forgotten by one's contractor, there is nothing more painful for a spirit who chose someone, I suppose."

"Gwaaaah! A sharp pain came creeping in slowly...! Beako, I'm sorry!!"

Picking up Beatrice as she slowly shook her head, Subaru frantically rubbed his cheek against hers.

From Beatrice's perspective, the duration might have been brief, but the fact remained that for a time, because his 'Memories' were devoured, Subaru had forgotten his contract with her.

However, precisely because he could understand that pain, Subaru could also rethink the situation.

"Right now, how are Tiga and Pooka perceiving things? Originally, Tiga joined the 'Beloved Children' for the sake of Melty-chan who was there, right? But now, Melty-chan isn't there. The reason has been left hanging in midair."

"...I don't know. It's just, Pooka was looking for her contractor... for 'Black Dog'. If so, I wondered if maybe Tiga was also... that is what I thought, but..."

"Melty-chan..."

Smiling weakly with a touch of bitterness, Melty spoke of the fleeting hope that had not been granted.

Reuniting with Tiga after being torn apart in an undesired manner—Melty had harbored a one-in-a-million hope in that. But sadly, that wish had not come true.

That was the whole truth behind the two of them passing each other by in the castle's basement.

"...What do you want to do, Melty-chan?"

Having taken in, digested, and understood the circumstances she carried, Subaru asked her that.

Melty leaving the 'Beloved Children', joining the 'Six Tongues', and aiming to crush Capella's scheme was, of course, driven by securing her own safety and the sense of duty belonging to one who knew the plan. However, having learned of these circumstances now, Subaru felt that wasn't all. ――No, it wasn't that he felt it. He desired for it not to be just that.

Natsuki Subaru already liked Melty Pristis.

And it was the creed of the easily smitten Natsuki Subaru to be as greedy as he could on behalf of the people he liked, and to want them to be happy.

Therefore――

"If there's something you want to do, Melty-chan, I'll help you with anything."

"――. Are you truly not bewitched by me? Subaru-san."

"Not at all! 'Cause there are plenty of number ones in my heart...!"

"Subaru is always serious, in fact. ...That is why it is troublesome, and that is why you should not shoulder too much either, I suppose."

Still being held up for the cheek-rubbing, Beatrice murmured that with a sigh. Taking in a breath at those words, Melty let slip, "'Librarian'-san..."

To that, Beatrice shrugged her shoulders,

"Not 'Librarian', Beatrice is fine, in fact. Betty will also call you Melty instead of 'White Sheep', I suppose."

"Ah... somehow, it feels like I'm the one who's going to be bewitched by the two of you."

"Well, Beako's cuteness is Evil Eye-class, after all."

"Then the foulness of Subaru's eyes is Evil Eye-class as well, in fact."

"That's not a compliment, is it?! Aren't you just telling me I have the eyes of a demon?!"

"Ahah."

At the compliments missing their mark, Melty inadvertently covered her mouth and laughed. Then, giving herself over to the impulse to laugh for a moment, she finally let out a long breath,

"――Subaru-san, Beatrice-san."

"Yeah."

"What is it, I suppose?"

Firmly clasping her hands in front of her stomach, Melty straightened her back, facing them. Keenly feeling the determination dwelling within those round eyes, he waited for her words.

There were things that could be communicated without putting them into words. Even so, important things had to be stated aloud.

Just as one told someone precious that they loved them, the things one had resolved to accomplish no matter what had to be proclaimed to the world.

Therefore――

"――There is a life that I want to take back, no matter what. And in that life, there is someone I want by my side. In order to take that person back, please lend me your strength."

"Yeah, sure thing. Let's do it together. Fate――"

"――Bring it on, in fact."

Her eyes widening at Subaru and Beatrice as they firmly thrust out their fists, Melty then nodded with renewed enthusiasm and gently touched both of her hands to their fists.

――It was a modest, yet unwavering declaration of resolve from Melty Pristis.
